.TH CBMAP_CONSTRUCT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_construct \- type-inferred BST map construction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

cbmap_construct(hm_name, key_type, val_type);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-inferred macro that creates a BST map with the default settings.
The macro finds the key type by itself: a signed integer, an unsigned
integer, a floating-point type, a string or another type. It also
creates type marker variables, which give the declared key type and the
declared value type to the other type-dispatching macros at each place
that calls them.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name   Name of the BST map variable to create
key_type  Type of the keys
val_type  Type of the values
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro stops the program if an allocation fails
The macro uses the default memory management and the default
comparison
For a struct key_type, the macro uses a raw memcmp order. See
cbmap_create_full(3) for the rules of the default comparison and for
how to give a custom_comparison_proc instead. The cbmap_construct_cc
macro is the type-inferred equivalent for a struct key_type
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cbmap_construct(map, int, char*);
int key = 42;
cbmap_insert(map, key, "hello");
cbmap_destroy(map);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_create (3),
.BR cbmap_create_full (3)
